{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/730786-a-packs-homestead","id":730786,"title":"A packs homestead","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-26T19:29:39-07:00","id":730786,"title":"A packs homestead","content":"somethings hit me a while ago Living apart from your pack is a renown loss?<br /> <br /> So what could a household look like?<br /> <br /> Anywhere from a shoddy Tenament, a farmhouse, a Gated community, or a Penthouse?<br /> <br /> unless a packs composed entirely of Red talons their likely going to want some kind of dwelling.<br /> <br /> But anything but a large mansion or a house in the country could raise ... questions about 4 or 5 people with no familial connection living together.<br /> <br /> Ideas how to explain it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T19:47:59-07:00","id":730869,"title":"","content":"I usually use the roommates idea. The pack rents a house or with appropriate resources buys one. In my last chronicle the pack inherited a mansion outside of a college town on acres of land. The players and storyteller should work together to create/find a suitable place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T19:51:08-07:00","id":730877,"title":"","content":"I would not take that too strictly literal. They don't need to live in the same structure as long as they are living in the same community and interact on a near daily basis. The prohibition is more for people who are technically pack members yet live apart - some guy being a hermit in the mountains while his packmates live in some other area. Homids would be more lenient in their definition than lupus whose natural pack structure keeps them together constantly.<br /> <br /> Use your judgment here - is the lone guy really part of the pack in the sense he's working together and being part of the family and sharing their lives together, or is he a pack member in name only whose life is actually different from the rest of them.<br /> <br /> Packmates are supposed to be like family, and this rule is meant to make sure they are acting like family. In the past, multi-generational households were common, but in the common day families are more spread out with their own homes and such. However, a family that lives near each other are likely to be closer together than ones whose members are spread out far enough that they can't interact and support one another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T21:45:37-07:00","id":731228,"title":"","content":"do boarding houses like on the anime &quot;Maison ikkoku&quot; still exist in real life?&quot; Just curious... then again a place like that is near constant provocation to frenzy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T00:39:32-07:00","id":731546,"title":"","content":"My player's pack is not far from an Iron Rider sept, and there are plenty of kinfolk in the community. Most of the Garou live in their own homes, sometimes with their families when duty permits, while others are often absent due to umbra quests or journeys to other Caerns and the like. None of these civilized Garou live at the Caern full-time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T01:36:19-07:00","id":731672,"title":"","content":"The idea of the renown loss is to punish the &quot;Lone Wolves&quot; from avoiding their own. It doesn't mean the pack has to live together in the same house. Heck, I'd say that considering that most Garou have families and tend towards high stress, they'd need a bit of time apart from each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T21:15:12-07:00","id":733843,"title":"","content":"oh for silent striders? Is it legitimate for those who travel a circuit to have a spouse on each leg of the circuit, or is that silly? <br /> <br /> brought the idea in for a dark ages game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T04:45:46-07:00","id":734338,"title":"","content":"Depends on his views on monogamy and polygamy and how his families can cope with their being multiples. It's also important to note that Striders in packs aren't usually on a circuit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T05:00:16-07:00","id":734354,"title":"","content":"I'd personally not take any of the Renown Chart suggestions as canon. They are meant to be suggestions how to give out renown, not examples how a garou should behave in the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T06:07:15-07:00","id":734460,"title":"","content":"I've seen this done a few ways. A lupus shadow lord who had their own den demanded...lead...his pack to building their own dens nearby. After a battle or receiving injuries he'd have them all in his recovering together to strengthen the bonds of pack. <br /> <br /> Homid child of gaia had a tent. The rest of pack started building more tents or shelter around it under a canopy of trees. Eventually it was like a huge den of throws, pillows, cushions, candles and incense (and a few kin) under natural camouflage and became known as the 'smoke house' where anyone could come and go as they pleased.<br /> <br /> Bonegnawers in an old junk yard made a shanty town within the rubble and debris from the old rubble debris that was formed by the oldest pieces of junk so it had a reflection in the umbra too.<br /> <br /> a pack lead by an Uktena had a long house. A very long cabin with a hearth at the far end.<br /> <br /> but mostly I've seen others build cabins for their packs to dwell. Urrah seem popular on having a whole floor in an appartment block dedicated to kin to Garou.<br /> <br /> I think a key component could be to base it around concepts that follow the breed and lifestyle, or sentiments and dedication either the pack hold and share or at least can identify with and appreciate.<br /> <br /> As for renown I do use the suggestions. ..as they are suggested. But also encourage other behaviours and deeds to be included in loss or gain determined by the expectations of the sept, pack and tribal totems of the chatacters too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T09:53:49-08:00","id":756697,"title":"","content":"oh idea just hit me?<br /> <br /> If you live in a RV or Yacht<br /> <br /> (followers of Shark or Dolphin could EASILY live in a yacht!) <br /> <br /> How to ensure theirs no serious damage to the functionality after a frenzy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T11:02:01-08:00","id":756936,"title":"","content":"what could a household look like?<br /> <br /> In the games I've played in and/or run this hasn't every really been an issue. Most of the games took place in rural areas, where the packs lived in a large house with neighbors a few miles away. Having 5-6 people living in a house that aren't related doesn't draw anywhere near as much attention as it would have even just a couple of decades ago. So having decent sized a house with 4 bedrooms or so was plenty to live comfortably. Generally the house was within running distance (for a wolf) to the caern in case something happened.<br /> In the one game we had that took place in a city, the local glasswalkers had purchased an apartment building and set it aside for packs and kinfolk. The walls were sound proofed and aside from a few frenzy incidents, there really weren't any issues. And even with frenzy, the pack was in charge of controlling the errant packmate.<br /> <br /> But agreeing with some above statements, even if the pack didn't want to live in the same household, as long as they were within relatively quick travel distance I wouldn't see any issue with it from a (Garou) societal point of view.<br /> <br /> I do think an RV might be too cramped for anything but the smallest (2-3 member) packs. RVs would work quite well for a ratkin pack though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T11:07:29-08:00","id":756946,"title":"","content":"Yachts?<br /> <br /> as If your constantly trying to prevent oceanic dumping...<br /> <br /> or you could all be crew on a ship?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 11-05-2015, 05:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T11:20:14-08:00","id":762445,"title":"","content":"We had a large, extended Silver Fang family living in a large, multi wing &quot;castle&quot; with outbuildings for guests. It was located in the bawn for the local Caern. It eventually became the focal point for part of the campaign and we had floor plans for the whole place and a fairly extensive history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Lead Writer for the Savage Age of Werewolf: the Apocalypse: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/428750/Ghost-Lineages-The-Advanced-Players-Guide-to-the-Savage-Age\" target=\"_blank\">Ghost Lineages</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/312700/The-Rise-of-the-Garou-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Two\" target=\"_blank\">Rise of the Garou</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/331302/Tools-of-Extinction-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Three\" target=\"_blank\">Tools of Extinction</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/352717/Tribebook-Wlewa\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook: Wlewa</a>.<br /> <br /> Want RPGs in libraries? Check out my book, <a href=\"http://www.abc-clio.com/ABC-CLIOCorporate/product.aspx?pc=A3951P\" target=\"_blank\">Dragons in the Stacks</a>. Now with <a href=\"http://www.ennie-awards.com/blog/2015-ennie-award-nominees-and-spotlight-winners/\" target=\"_blank\">awards</a>!<br /> \u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1813-grimjaws","name":"grimjaws","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1813_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T08:57:50-08:00","id":803785,"title":"","content":"Oh curious, ideas on precautions,to take, on anything upscale, from penthouse to country manor, to keep damage from potential frenzys to a MININUM? any ideas?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T11:36:20-08:00","id":803882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/730786-a-packs-homestead?p=803785#post803785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh curious, ideas on precautions,to take, on anything upscale, from penthouse to country manor, to keep damage from potential frenzys to a MININUM? any ideas?</div> </div> </div> </div>Bubble wrap","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T12:02:50-08:00","id":803905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/730786-a-packs-homestead?p=803785#post803785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh curious, ideas on precautions,to take, on anything upscale, from penthouse to country manor, to keep damage from potential frenzys to a MININUM? any ideas?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think maybe Frenzies happen a lot more in other people's games than I am used to.<br /> From my perspective, there doesn't need to be precautions in place. Garou are expected to maintain control of themselves. Losing oneself to Frenzy results in renown loss after all.<br /> Aside from that, the Garou's own pack and/or Elders are around to prevent damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T12:17:58-08:00","id":803922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/730786-a-packs-homestead?p=803905#post803905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think maybe Frenzies happen a lot more in other people's games than I am used to.<br /> From my perspective, there doesn't need to be precautions in place. Garou are expected to maintain control of themselves. Losing oneself to Frenzy results in renown loss after all.<br /> Aside from that, the Garou's own pack and/or Elders are around to prevent damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Frenzies happen pretty much how often players request a frenzy check. So in some games its very common while in others its rarer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T23:34:24-08:00","id":804276,"title":"","content":"In my game frenzies are fairly common within the context of combat, but my players have yet to frenzy in their homes and harm their loved ones or possessions; perhaps that is is an oversight and I need to inject more soap-opera drama into their home lives to infuriate them :P <br /> <br /> Most of the time the damage inflicted on the environment is small potatoes compared to the loss of life and limb (frenzied Garou seem to prioritize attacking living things, not objects, after all).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T06:34:20-08:00","id":804416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/730786-a-packs-homestead?p=804276#post804276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my game frenzies are fairly common within the context of combat, but my players have yet to frenzy in their homes and harm their loved ones or possessions; perhaps that is is an oversight and I need to inject more soap-opera drama into their home lives to infuriate them :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much this. I call for Frenzy checks often enough I think. But it tends to come up most during combat. Frenzies have happened here and there outside of combat, but that's fairly atypical. If and when it does happen, the character/player generally spends willpower to buy time to get the hell out of there and/or get their Rage under control.<br /> And of course, as the Garou rise in rank, the threat or Frenzy lessens anyway. Almost all non combat Frenzies I've dealt with (as a player and as a ST) were when dealing with Rank 1 or 2 Garou.<br /> <br /> Also worth noting, even when calling for a Frenzy check, it is far from guaranteed the character will Frenzy. Depending on circumstances, the likelihood of getting 4 successes on a Rage roll can vary wildly. Experience teaches both players and characters to manage those circumstances and adjust accordingly.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T06:54:26-08:00","id":804426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/730786-a-packs-homestead?p=804416#post804416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty much this. I call for Frenzy checks often enough I think. But it tends to come up most during combat. Frenzies have happened here and there outside of combat, but that's fairly atypical. If and when it does happen, the character/player generally spends willpower to buy time to get the hell out of there and/or get their Rage under control.<br /> And of course, as the Garou rise in rank, the threat or Frenzy lessens anyway. Almost all non combat Frenzies I've dealt with (as a player and as a ST) were when dealing with Rank 1 or 2 Garou.<br /> <br /> Also worth noting, even when calling for a Frenzy check, it is far from guaranteed the character will Frenzy. Depending on circumstances, the likelihood of getting 4 successes on a Rage roll can vary wildly. Experience teaches both players and characters to manage those circumstances and adjust accordingly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, in a lot of games I've played, players call frenzy checks when character is angered. And given a lot of these are chats/forum rps, they can happen anywhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-01T19:29:02-07:00","id":879848,"title":"","content":"Sorry for Threadomancy but wanted to ask... what level would an immobile Fetish that prevented frenzys ni a specific structure probaly be?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-01T23:36:50-07:00","id":879941,"title":"","content":"Well, there is a Rite that raises all Rage difficulty to 9, and there are gifts ending Frenzy, like Dazzle, at rank 3. Working in one structure (of reasonable size, like a one family home) I would go for level 3 or 4.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T13:39:22-07:00","id":881228,"title":"","content":"so in a mansion about 5.<br /> <br /> as that where you'd be most worried with a lot of ming vases and such.<br /> <br /> Though im sure the Fangs, and Glasswalkers have worked out multiple ways to minimalize damage when a frenzy does occur... Ideas What a glasswalker can tell Insurance happened to his Apartment, after he tore it up in a frenzy? <br /> <br /> &quot;A crime syndicate attacked!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\"