"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T05:52:02-07:00","id":882798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/730786-a-packs-homestead?p=882726#post882726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am basing that statement, on a novel I read years ago And a Documentary I watched on the Samurai in high school.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I've seen documentaries on magical ninja powers. What's your point? Just because someone thinks it makes for good drama, doesn't mean that's how it worked. The intricacies of the clan politics and marriage as well as courting the favour of the Daimyo and the Shogun were downright byzantine. I would suggest reading up on it a bit more as it makes for some insane reading (especially the stuff about the court drama, vying for favour and arranged marriages and how they make everyone miserable). <b>Samurai, Warfare and the State in Early Medieval Japan</b> by Karl Friday is great, and if you're in for lighter reading <b>Usagi Yojimbo</b> is always brilliant, well researched and the footnotes will really help you with comprehending the society.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg"